<a name="2026-11-05-the-blue-tsunami"> </a>
<h3>The Blue Tsunami</h3>
<p>As has been widely discussed in the news, Democrats have had
 incredible gains in Tuesday’s elections. Even <em>Texas</em> turned
 blue this election cycle, something not seen for decades. In fact, <a href="AI/2026-11-05-Motte.html">this 2024 → 2026 shift is the  biggest two year shift with voters since the 1930s, with people voting  some 17% more blue in 2026 than they did  in 2024</a>.
<p>Republican Vice President JD Vance has an <a href="AI/2026-11-05-Vance.html">excellent summary</a> 
of what happened. He says that ending the Iran war
 is important, reducing inflation is also important, as well as putting
 America first and reassessing our relationship with Israel. I generally
 agree with him; I have a friend who I was talking to the day before the
 election; she asked me who to vote for. I told her to vote straight
 Blue (Democrat) because the war on Iran was increasing gas prices, but
 to vote against the wealth tax, because that passing would destroy
 California’s economy.
<p>This is definitely <em>not</em> a mandate for leftist “culture war”
 causes. Blue Washington state <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Washington_Initiative_638">looks to be passing an initiative forbidding biological males on female sport teams</a>, 
and liberal California <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_California_Proposition_40">looks to have voted against a wealth tax for  billionaires</a>. 
As
 Clinton said in 1992, “It’s the economy, stupid”. Indeed, Texas’s
 Democrat governor-elect <a href="AI/2026-11-05-Hinojosa.html">doesn’t want a culture war</a>. 
As it turns out, <a href="AI/2026-11-05-JeffMaurer.html">candidates endorsed by  leftist Sanders did worse than candidates not endorsed by Sanders</a>.
<p>Point being, the Republicans went too far with an unwanted war in
 Iran. Democrats have a chance to hold on to power by giving voters what
 they want: That means improving the economy, <em>not</em> engaging in
 an unwanted culture war and <em>not</em> trying to make America a
 leftist state.
<a name="2026-11-05-mating-puzzle-solution"> </a>
<h3>Mating puzzle solution</h3>
<p>1. Bb5+! Kb6 2. Bxd4+ c5 3. Qxc5#


